TITLE:: ImagerView
summary:: Imager's display: the bands' widths, their correlations, and the image
categories:: Libraries>Imager
related:: Classes/Imager, Classes/FxParamView, Classes/FxDevicePanel

DESCRIPTION::
What link::Classes/FxDevicePanel:: puts at the top of link::Classes/Imager::'s window, with the meters beside it.

Left, the band plane: frequency along on a log scale, each band a column between its splits, in its colour (violet, teal, lime, gold, low to high). Up from the middle line is wider, down narrower to mono: the band's bar is its code::width::, and an apricot cap over it how much side code::stereo:: adds. The band the panel shows is framed; with a band soloed, the others are drawn faint. Under the bars, each band's correlation, the last five seconds of it: +1 is mono, 0 two unrelated sides, under 0 the sides fight and the band thins out in mono. The number is the correlation now, the dim tick what came in.

Right, the image: the output as dots, middle up and side across, so a mono sound is a vertical line, left at the upper left and right at the upper right. The words over it choose the drawing (code::scopeMode::):

table::
## code::\dots:: || polar, folded into a half circle: the 45 degree lines are hard left and hard right, and dots past them are out of phase
## code::\lissajous:: || the dots as they come
## code::\level:: || the loudest dot in each direction, as rays
::

Under the image, the correlation of the whole output, -1 to +1.

table::
## strong::in the display:: || strong::does::
## click a band || shows its controls in the band card (code::focusAction::)
## drag a band up and down || its code::width::
## the wheel on a band || its code::stereo::
## drag a split line || moves the split
## click dots, lissajous, level || how the image is drawn
## shift || fine, a tenth as far
## double click || back to the default of what is under it
::

The bars and splits are the settings. The correlations, the dots and the bar under the image are what the server measures (the object's code::extras::, see link::Classes/Imager#*extrasSize::): they move only while the window is running, and the dots show the effect's output before code::mix:: and code::output::.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: unit
The link::Classes/Imager::.
ARGUMENT:: parent

METHOD:: historySize
How many correlation values are kept per band: 125, five seconds at 25 replies a second.

METHOD:: trail
How many meter replies of dots stay on screen: 6.

METHOD:: scopeModes
code::[\dots, \lissajous, \level]::.

METHOD:: fold
A point of the image, code::[side, middle]::, folded into the upper half: under the middle line it is the same direction, upside down.
ARGUMENT:: p

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: focus
The band shown, from 0; the panel sets it, and a click in a band sets it back through code::focusAction::.

METHOD:: focusAction
A Function of the band clicked, from 0.

METHOD:: scopeMode
How the image is drawn: one of link::#*scopeModes::.

METHOD:: levelsArrived
Called on every meter reply: keeps the correlations and the dots.

METHOD:: hint
What is under the pointer, for the hint bar.
ARGUMENT:: x
ARGUMENT:: y
